The paper’s exact object is a family of \(n\) edge-matchings in one bipartite graph; Theorem 2.1 guarantees a full rainbow matching when every color class has size \(\lfloor5n/3\rfloor\). The proof is existential via a maximum partial rainbow matching, not an explicit one-line certificate. I’m now checking whether its promised regime yields a genuinely difficult search distribution or whether the slack makes standard exact-cover search trivial.
